text_en:
Article 37-13 (Prohibition on discriminative payment of subsidies)
A mobile communications business operator, agent, or sales store shall not, under Article 32-12(1) of the Act, provide or propose to provide different subsidies to users for the same subscription type, rate plan, and mobile communications terminal device based on the grounds listed in the following subparagraphs:
The user's place of residence, including the address;
The user's age;The user’s physical condition, such as a disability.
Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the provision of preferential subsidies for a specified period to the following persons shall not be considered unfair discrimination:
Persons residing in islands and remote areas as defined in Article 2 of the Act on the Promotion of Education in Islands and Remote Areas;
Senior citizens eligible for preferential treatment under Article 26 of the Welfare of Senior Citizens Act;
Persons with disabilities registered under Article 32 of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
Other individuals whom the Korea Media Communications Commission recognizes eligible for a subsidy to be provided for a specified period and designates by public notice.
[This Article Added on Apr. 28, 2026]
[Previous Article 37-13 moved to Article 37-21 <Jan. 3, 2023>]

sub_chunks.content:
Article 37-13 (Prohibition on discriminative payment of subsidies)
A mobile communications business operator, agent, or sales store shall not, under Article 32-12(1) of the Act, provide or propose to provide different subsidies to users for the same subscription type, rate plan, and mobile communications terminal device based on the grounds listed in the following subparagraphs:
The user's place of residence, including the address;
The user's age;The user’s physical condition, such as a disability.
Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the provision of preferential subsidies for a specified period to the following persons shall not be considered unfair discrimination:
Persons residing in islands and remote areas as defined in Article 2 of the Act on the Promotion of Education in Islands and Remote Areas;
Senior citizens eligible for preferential treatment under Article 26 of the Welfare of Senior Citizens Act;
Persons with disabilities registered under Article 32 of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
Other individuals whom the Korea Media Communications Commission recognizes eligible for a subsidy to be provided for a specified period and designates by public notice.
[This Article Added on Apr. 28, 2026]
[Previous Article 37-13 moved to Article 37-21 <Jan. 3, 2023>]

text_en:
Article 37-14 (Creation of fair distribution environment)
The policy measures necessary to foster a sound distribution environment under Article 32-13(7) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as “policy measures” in this Article) shall include the following:
Matters prescribed in Article 32-13(1) through (5) of the Act;
Measures for monitoring the distribution market for mobile communications terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules for mobile communications terminal devices (hereafter referred to as “mobile communication terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules” in this Article);
Matters necessary to ensure fair competition, such as improving access to information regarding users’ mobile communications terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules, and enhancing their choice rights;
Matters related to the prevention, education, and remediation of user harm in the distribution market for mobile communication terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules;
Matters concerning the promotion and support of self-regulatory activities by mobile communications terminal device manufacturers, mobile communications business operators, or related organizations;
Any other matters deemed necessary by the Korea Media and Communications Commission to foster a sound distribution environment for mobile communications terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules.
The consultative body established under Article 32-13(10) of the Act (hereafter referred to as the “distribution environment improvement council” in this Article) shall consist of up to 15 members, including mobile communications business operators, mobile communications terminal device manufacturers, executive officers and employees of relevant institutions or organizations, experts, and public officials.
The distribution environment improvement council shall perform the following duties:
Monitoring the market and gathering feedback to establish policy measures;
Proposing measures to ensure compliance with policy measures, inspecting the status of implementation of policy measures, and recommending improvements;
Proposing implementation measures regarding the recommendations to improve distribution conditions under Article 32-13(8) of the Act;
Other suggestions necessary for fostering a sound distribution environment for mobile communications terminal devices and universal subscriber identity modules.
The Korea Media and Communications Commission may provide the necessary support for the operation of the distribution environment improvement council.
The Korea Media and Communications Commission may, where necessary in connection with the formulation and implementation of policy measures and the provision of support under paragraph (4), request cooperation, such as the submission of materials or opinions, from the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the heads of local governments, relevant institutions and organizations, mobile communications business operators, and mobile communications terminal device manufacturers.
Except as provided in paragraphs (2) through (5), the Korea Media and Communications Commission shall determined necessary matters relating to the composition and operation of the distribution environment improvement council.
[This Article Added on Apr. 28, 2026]

