text_en:
Article 37-15 (Matters to be specified in contracts for mobile communication terminal devices)
“Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree” in Article 32-15(3) of the Act refers to the following matters:
Contract details and installment terms related to the mobile communications terminal device, including the model name, manufacturer’s suggested retail price, ex-factory prices, principal balance, installment fees, and monthly payments;
Details of the subsidy, including the paying entity and payment method;
The contract term for mobile communications services, rate plan, and the names and charges of associated value-added services;
The following matters relating to the rate plan or associated value-added services:
a.
Mandatory term of use;
b.
Terms and conditions for cancellation or modification;
c.
Charges arising from early termination or modification (including the repayment of the subsidies);
Whether the service is combined with any of the following services, and the conditions for payment of related subsidies;
a.
Internet subscriber access service;
b.
Pay broadcast as defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Broadcasting Act;
c.
Internet multimedia broadcasting as defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Internet Multimedia Broadcasting Business Act;
d.
Other telecommunications services, and broadcasting as defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Broadcasting Act;
Other conditions attached to the subsidies.
[This Article Added on Apr. 28, 2026]

