A person who believes that a mobile communications business operator has engaged in conduct in violation of Article 32-11(1) or Article 32-15(1) of this Act may report such conduct to the Minister of Science and ICT.
A person who believes that a mobile communications business operator (including its affiliated companies), an agent, a sales store, or a mobile communication terminal device manufacturer has violated any of the following subparagraphs may report such facts to the Korea Media and Communications Commission:
Article 32-12(1) of the Act;
Article 32-12(2), (3), and (5) of the Act;
Article 32-14(1), (3), and (5) of the Act;
Article 32-15(2) and 3 of the Act.
A person intending to file a report under paragraph (1) or (2) shall submit a document containing the following information:
The reporting person’s name and address (in the case of a corporation, this refers to the corporation’s name and address, as well as the name and address of its representative);
The trade name or name and address of the respondent (in the case of a corporation, this refers to the corporation’s name and address, as well as the name and address of its representative);
The details of the violation.
Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), the matters necessary for the procedures for processing reports and other related matters shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT and the Korea Media and Communications Commission.
[This Article Added on Apr. 28, 2026]

