Article 37-21 (Notice of suspension of telecommunications services)
Where the provision of telecommunications services has been suspended, a telecommunications business operator shall notify, without delay, users of the suspension of the provision thereof, the cause of the suspension, status of responsive measures taken, contact information on receipt of relevant consultations, etc. under Article 33(2) of the Act; provided, this shall not apply to any of the following cases: <Amended on Mar. 28, 2025>
Where the provision of telecommunications services has been suspended to replace telecommunications equipment or to improve services, within the scope of a prior notice given;
Where the provision of telecommunications services has been suspended due to a failure in telecommunications line equipment of a facilities-based telecommunications business operator;
Where the provision of any of the following value-added telecommunications services has been suspended:
a.
Value-added telecommunications services provided by persons whose sales of telecommunications services in the previous year is less than 10 billion won;
b.
Value-added telecommunications services with an average daily user count of less than one million over the three months immediately preceding the end of the previous year;
Deleted; <Mar. 28, 2025>
Where the provision of telecommunications services is interrupted within 2 hours due to any of the following unforeseen and unavoidable reasons; provided, this shall not apply where the provision of telecommunications services is interrupted due to a malfunction or error in critical communications facilities (referring to facilities designated as broadcasting communications facilities specified in Article 35(2)1 of the Framework Act on Broadcasting Communications Development according to a master plan for the management of disasters in broadcasting communications formulated under paragraph (1) of that Article):
a.
Where the use of telecommunications services is excessively concentrated;
b.
Where a telecommunications equipment failure or error occurs;
c.
Where any situation corresponding to item a or b occurs, such as an abnormal phenomenon occurring in software for providing telecommunications services;
Where the provision of cloud computing services prescribed in the Act on the Development of Cloud Computing and Protection of Its Users has been suspended.
Where the provision of telecommunication services is interrupted, a telecommunications business operator shall, under Article 33(2) of the Act, notify users of the following matters within 30 days from the date on which the provision of telecommunication services is resumed or the cause of the disruption is resolved; provided, the foregoing shall not apply where any of the circumstances specified in paragraph (1) 1 through 3 and 5 applies, and where telecommunications services provided to users without any user charge payable on a monthly or other periodic basis have been interrupted: <Amended on Mar. 28, 2025>
The person entitled to claim compensation;
The standards for compensation for damages;
The procedures and methods for compensation for damages.
Where providing notice under paragraph (1) or (2), the telecommunications business operator shall do so using one or more of the following methods; provided, where it is difficult to provide notice using telecommunications facilities regarding the fact that the provision of telecommunications services has been suspended, the operator shall inform the media of the suspension without delay and then immediately provide notice in accordance with under the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of paragraph (1) as soon as it becomes possible to provide notice by each of the following methods: <Amended on Mar. 28, 2025>
Using e-mails;Using text messages;
Posting such interruption on the relevant website or on the access screens of applications used in mobile communication terminal devices;
Using electronic notification methods that can individually inform users, such as social network services (SNS);
Where a telecommunications business operator may follow a separate notification method that has been predetermined when entering into a contract with the user, notwithstanding paragraph (3).
[This Article Added on Jun. 25, 2019]
[Moved from Article 37-13 <Apr. 28, 2026>]
CHAPTER IV PROMOTION OF COMPETITION BETWEEN TELECOMMUNICATIONS BUSINESSES

