text_en:
Article 38-2 (Subject matters and details of fact-finding surveys of value-added telecommunications business)
The subject matters of a fact-finding survey to identify the current status of value-added telecommunications business under Article 34-2(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "fact-finding survey") shall be as follows: <Amended on Apr. 28, 2026>
A person who has filed a report on value-added telecommunications business pursuant to Article 22(1) of the Act;
A person who has filed for registration of value-added telecommunications business pursuant to Article 22(2) of the Act;
A person who is deemed to have filed a report on value-added telecommunications business pursuant to Article 22(5) of the Act.
The details of a fact-finding survey shall be as follows:
General status, such as business registration number, the name of the representative, trade name or title, and the location of the main office;
Financial status, such as capital, sales, and operating incomes;
Current status of and demand for human resources, such as the number of employees and the number of persons to be employed;
Current status of research and development or technologies, including research and development expenses, the number of intellectual property rights, and a plan for utilizing new technology;
Current status of the provision of value-added telecommunications services, such as the details of services provided, the number of service users, the number of transactions, and transaction amounts;
Current status of the protection and use of data, such as the types of data collected according to the provision of value-added telecommunications services and the types of use of data collected;
Current status of the competition in value-added telecommunications services, including market share, and company acquisition and mergers;
Other matters deemed by the Minister of Science and ICT as necessary to identify the current status of value-added telecommunications business.
The Minister of Science and ICT shall conduct a fact-finding survey once each year.
Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to conduct a fact-finding survey, he or she shall formulate a plan for fact-finding survey, including the purpose and subjects of the fact-finding survey, the standards for selecting the subjects, and the details, methods, period, etc. thereof, and shall inform persons subject to the fact-finding survey in writing no later than 30 days before commencing such fact-finding survey.
Before conducting a fact-finding survey, the Minister of Science and ICT shall hear in advance opinions from the relevant experts and interested parties.
A fact-finding survey shall be conducted through an interview, field survey, document survey, statistical survey, literature survey, etc. and may be conducted through the information and communications networks or electronically, such as via electronic mails, if necessary for conducting the survey efficiently.
The Minister of Science and ICT may request necessary data from the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies, the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor/ Do Governor"), companies, research institutes, or other public institutions or organizations.
Documents referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 29(1) and (2);

