text_en:
Where the Minister of Science and ICT prepares a mediation proposal, upon receipt of a request for mediation under Article 68(5) of the Act, he or she shall hear opinions of the heads of the relevant administrative agencies and the relevant parties. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
Where the Minister of Science and ICT has prepared a mediation proposal under paragraph (1), he or she shall notify the relevant parties of such mediation proposal and may recommend them to accept such mediation proposal with a fixed period of at least 30 days. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
Where the relevant parties accept a mediation proposal under paragraph (2), the Minister of Science and ICT shall prepare a mediation proposal in which the following matters are entered and have the relevant parties affix their seals or signatures thereon: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
The number of a case;
The name and address of the relevant parties, appointed representatives or agents;
The intent of a request for mediation;
Items of mediation;The date of preparation.
[This Article Wholly Amended on Feb. 28, 2012]
[Moved from Article 51-12 <Jan. 19, 2024>]

